data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":91,"item_id":"rs_04476f8fd520e151016aca0c1a22f48193bed41572ad1b6f84","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering test appending methods**\n\nI'm thinking about how to append tests using bash. Should I write only the new ones or rewrite existing entries? Maybe using edit and appending only allows me to focus on the last block uniquely. I'm wondering if I should create a new, separate test instead of appending directly. It seems importing helpers or triggers for tests could be okay too, but maybe focusing on small, unique endings could be the key. I'm weighing my options!"}

